  "shared_boundary_question": {
    "instructions": {
      "task": "Is enough local target treatment supplied to judge this utterance and circumstance connection? Context cannot supply omitted address. This does not certify complete episode boundaries.",
      "boundary": "Judge only candidate.utterance in target_text, using the surrounding target to interpret it. Other target sentences do not supply an act absent from this utterance. Leading/trailing context may identify a referent but cannot supply an act or circumstance connection. Reported/rejected person-directed acts can exist without preacher adoption. Address to God is not address to a person. No opposite act is synthesized from rejection. Each question is independent; no empathy, outcome, pastor trait or quality judgment. Preserve conditions and limits in the source, not as inferred benefit."
    },
    "criteria": {
      "local_sufficient": "Enough local evidence to decide, including definite absence of address/binding.",
      "continuation_required": "Required act, connection or referent remains outside target evidence.",
      "unclear": "Local sufficiency unresolved."
    }
  },
  "scope_finding": "Shared utterance-and-circumstance sufficiency is broader than the exported atomic-act claim; causal reason for model withholding is unestablished.",
  "guardrails": {
    "measurements_immutable": true,
    "questions_unchanged": true,
    "threshold_unchanged": true,
    "G2_admission_unchanged": true,
    "no_V4_retroactive_PASS": true,
    "raw_provenance_required": true,
    "all_observed_acts_reviewed": true,
    "no_context_lent_act": true,
    "no_circumstance_claim": true,
    "original_quarantines_unchanged": true,
    "proposed_witness_has_no_authority": true
  },
  "atomic_route_requirements": [
    "New accepted policy/item/witness versions; never treat V4 review acceptance as A1 authority.",
    "Preserve receipt, model, questions, roles, phase isolation, source-envelope, accepted-review and export/deserialize/consume identity checks.",
    "Keep source context_complete and exact target_complete requirements; missing act, condition, referent or source introduction blocks. Full source outside supplied envelope cannot repair missing supplied evidence.",
    "Every actually observed act must already pass the frozen .80 measurement gate and have independent claim-specific source support in the exact utterance. Unknown acts remain unknown. Any unsupported positive blocks the row.",
    "Actual voice, addressee and adoption remain definite at .80, agree with reviewed origin, and satisfy the existing current/reported namespace rules. Review cannot replace unknown or incompatible measured provenance.",
    "Require a separately accepted receipt-bound claim-sufficiency witness enumerating the exact exported acts, role spans, conditions/limits, source and recipient identity evidence, source stance, completeness rationale and explicit exclusions. Generic target_complete alone is insufficient.",
    "For the atomic-only route, boundary may be gated local_sufficient or unclear; unclear supplies no positive sufficiency authority. A definite continuation_required or any other boundary decision blocks this route. Ignore low-probability argmax as an admission vote.",
    "Only the broader shared boundary requirement is replaced for this new route by affirmative claim-scoped sufficiency. No replacement of actual act/voice/recipient/adoption decisions or relationship decisions.",
    "Retain narration/God vetoes, null-circumstance consistency and rejection of unsupported positive relevance/binding. Withheld relations stay withheld; a raw relation disagreement cannot be hidden by omitting its export.",
    "Export only observed acts, exact utterance and conditions, provenanced current or reported namespace, atomic-only scope and review/policy identities. circumstance_claim, pastor_projection and quality_score remain null; circumstance pointers in raw roles confer no relation claim.",
    "Re-admit under the same accepted A1 authority on export, deserialization and consumption; old readers reject A1 schema and new readers cannot silently upgrade V4 items. No adapter or fallback may bypass sufficiency."
  ],
